1. Third-party content NOT included in this repository
------------------------------------------------------

The following items are excluded for copyright reasons or to satisfy GPL source
obligations. Obtain them yourself:

1.1 **AMD/Xilinx documentation**
    - PG245 Debug Bridge v2.0
    - XAPP1251 Xilinx Virtual Cable on Zynq-7000
    - UG908 Vivado Programming and Debugging
    - UG470 7 Series FPGAs Configuration
    - and any text extracted from the above (*.txt / *.mhtml / *.pdf)
    → download from https://docs.amd.com

1.2 **Zynq PS initialization code** `ps7_init.c/h`, `ps7_init_gpl.c/h`, `ps7_init.tcl`
    - Generated automatically by Vivado/PetaLinux from the XSA
    - The `*_gpl.*` files carry an explicit GPL notice
    → regenerated by `petalinux-build`; no need to commit them

1.3 **Bootable images** `BOOT.BIN`, `image.ub`
    - Embed the Linux kernel, busybox, glibc and other GPL/LGPL components
    - Distributing these binaries requires providing the complete corresponding source
    → this repository provides the **build sources**
      (petalinux/project-spec + apps); download the binaries from the Releases
      page, which also states how to obtain the sources

1.4 **Xilinx-generated Vivado project files** `*.xpr`, `*.hw/`, `*.runs/`, etc.
    → build artifacts; rebuild with `xvc/vivado/build_jtag12p.tcl`

1.5 **Vendor reference bundle** `references/`
    → vendor board documentation and PDFs; not committed

2. Generated artifacts included in this repository
--------------------------------------------------

- `xvc/out/v16/fpga/system.bit`
  - Produced by synthesizing and implementing this project's own RTL
    (`xvc/vivado/rtl/`)
  - It is the original design output of this project, used to configure the FPGA
  - Rebuild from source: `vivado -mode batch -source xvc/vivado/build_jtag12p.tcl`

